We say that $\mathcal{S}$ is \emph{phylogenetically decisive} if it satisfies the following property: If $T$ and $T$' are binary phylogenetic trees, with $T|Y=T$'$|Y$ for all $Y \in \mathcal{S}$, then $T=T$'. 
\end{defn}

